WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.266 --> 00:00:02.302 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Now, Donald Trump
does not like either of us,

00:00:02.302 --> 00:00:03.269 line:92%
but he might dislike you more

00:00:03.269 --> 00:00:06.239
because I tell jokes about him,
but you sue him.

00:00:06.239 --> 00:00:07.540 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Well...
-And sometimes --

00:00:07.540 --> 00:00:08.708 align:start size:94% position:6%
Sometimes,
you sue him to the point

00:00:08.708 --> 00:00:11.711 align:start size:94% position:6%
that he has to give up money,
and he likes that a lot.

00:00:11.711 --> 00:00:16.483
-No, but you mocked him
and humiliated him and his hair

00:00:16.483 --> 00:00:18.084 align:start size:94% position:6%
on national TV.
I don't know, Seth.

00:00:18.084 --> 00:00:20.320 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yeah. A little of both.
-It's a close call.

00:00:20.320 --> 00:00:23.356 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Uh, now,
you have sued him in the past.

00:00:23.356 --> 00:00:25.592 align:start size:94% position:6%
You sued Trump University
for fraud.

00:00:25.592 --> 00:00:27.660 align:start size:94% position:6%
He swore he would
never settle that.

00:00:27.660 --> 00:00:29.529 align:start size:94% position:6%
He was elected president.
He did settle it.

00:00:29.529 --> 00:00:32.899 align:start size:94% position:6%
Originally, you guys were
looking into Trump University

00:00:32.899 --> 00:00:33.833 line:92%
because you just wanted him

00:00:33.833 --> 00:00:35.335 size:78% position:39%
to take away the name
"university," right?

00:00:35.335 --> 00:00:38.238 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Well, we were looking at
for-profit colleges generally,

00:00:38.238 --> 00:00:40.740 size:88% position:44%
and there were problems
with for-profit colleges

00:00:40.740 --> 00:00:41.408 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
ripping people off.

00:00:41.408 --> 00:00:45.145
Actually, we've sued the Federal
Department of Education

00:00:45.145 --> 00:00:46.946
for trying to remove rules
that would protect students

00:00:46.946 --> 00:00:50.283 size:81% position:41%
from being ripped off
by for-profit colleges
a couple of weeks ago.

00:00:50.283 --> 00:00:52.419 align:start size:94% position:6%
And we were looking
at for-profit colleges,

00:00:52.419 --> 00:00:54.854 align:start size:94% position:6%
and there was Trump University
hanging out there,

00:00:54.854 --> 00:00:58.091 align:start size:94% position:6%
like, with a neon sign on it
saying "Fraud Here."

00:00:58.091 --> 00:01:02.996
And we attempted to negotiate
a settlement. That failed.

00:01:02.996 --> 00:01:05.398 align:start size:94% position:6%
And so, in the summer of 2013,
we sued him.

00:01:05.398 --> 00:01:09.002
And that's when our relationship
took a turn for the worst.

00:01:09.002 --> 00:01:09.602 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
-Yeah.

00:01:09.602 --> 00:01:13.673
He has mentioned you on Twitter
a couple of times...

00:01:13.673 --> 00:01:14.441 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
not very kindly.

00:01:14.441 --> 00:01:17.444 size:88% position:44%
Here's one. "Lightweight
A.G. Eric Schneiderman

00:01:17.444 --> 00:01:18.778 line:92%
is perhaps the most incompetent

00:01:18.778 --> 00:01:20.513 align:start size:94% position:6%
and least respected A.G.
in the U.S.

00:01:20.513 --> 00:01:21.915 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
He's a total joke."

00:01:21.915 --> 00:01:23.817 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
[ Laughter ]

00:01:23.817 --> 00:01:25.618 align:start size:94% position:6%
"Lightweight
@AGSchneiderman..."

00:01:25.618 --> 00:01:26.953 align:start size:94% position:6%
He used your Twitter handle
that time.

00:01:26.953 --> 00:01:28.521 size:88% position:44%
That's very -- He wanted
to make sure you saw it.

00:01:28.521 --> 00:01:30.890 align:start size:94% position:6%
"Just got his ass kicked
by Trump."

00:01:30.890 --> 00:01:32.559 line:92%
And, then, "It's Thursday."

00:01:32.559 --> 00:01:34.928 align:start size:94% position:6%
I like, by the way, when
he tells you what day it is.

00:01:34.928 --> 00:01:36.429 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
"It's Thursday.

00:01:36.429 --> 00:01:37.163 size:81% position:41% line:92%
What brand of eyeliner

00:01:37.163 --> 00:01:39.399 align:start size:94% position:6%
is the nation's worst A.G.
wearing today?"

00:01:39.399 --> 00:01:42.235 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yes.
-Now, do you take it as a...

00:01:42.235 --> 00:01:44.804
point of pride when someone like
this attacks you on Twitter?

00:01:44.804 --> 00:01:46.639 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Well, look,
it was very unusual.

00:01:46.639 --> 00:01:49.542 align:start size:94% position:6%
I mean, we sue a lot of people
for fraud.

00:01:49.542 --> 00:01:52.846 align:start size:94% position:6%
I'd never seen the sort of
scorched-earth approach

00:01:52.846 --> 00:01:53.613 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
he brought to it.

00:01:53.613 --> 00:01:56.216 align:start size:94% position:6%
He set up a website
to attack me,

00:01:56.216 --> 00:01:57.117 line:92%
sued me for $100 million,

00:01:57.117 --> 00:01:59.486 align:start size:94% position:6%
filed phony ethics complaints
against me.

00:01:59.486 --> 00:02:01.054 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
The full front page

00:02:01.054 --> 00:02:03.723 align:start size:94% position:6%
of his son-in-law's newspaper,
The Observer, was --

00:02:03.723 --> 00:02:04.724 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Oh, yes.
-Here you go.

00:02:04.724 --> 00:02:08.628
This is Jared Kushner's --
Jared Kushner's newspaper.

00:02:08.628 --> 00:02:10.697 line:92%
And that's you right there.

00:02:10.697 --> 00:02:12.599 line:92%
-That's me with the eyeliner

00:02:12.599 --> 00:02:14.267 align:start size:94% position:6%
as the Malcolm McDowell
character

00:02:14.267 --> 00:02:15.668 align:start size:94% position:6%
in "A Clockwork Orange."
-"Clockwork Eric."

00:02:15.668 --> 00:02:18.972
-So, in retrospect --
I didn't realize this in 2013 --

00:02:18.972 --> 00:02:20.707 align:start size:94% position:6%
I got a preview
of the scorched earth

00:02:20.707 --> 00:02:22.142 align:start size:94% position:6%
he brought to the campaign
last year,

00:02:22.142 --> 00:02:24.944 align:start size:94% position:6%
'cause before there was
Lyin' Ted and Little Marco,

00:02:24.944 --> 00:02:25.879 line:92%
there was Clockwork Eric.

00:02:25.879 --> 00:02:27.947 size:88% position:44%
But this is the approach
he brings to litigation

00:02:27.947 --> 00:02:29.048 align:start size:94% position:6%
and the approach
he brings to politics.

00:02:29.048 --> 00:02:32.218 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Now, no matter what happened
on election night,

00:02:32.218 --> 00:02:34.687
you were gonna have Donald Trump
in your life

00:02:34.687 --> 00:02:35.955 line:92%
because all his businesses --

00:02:35.955 --> 00:02:37.624 align:start size:94% position:6%
He has so much stuff
in New York.

00:02:37.624 --> 00:02:40.293 align:start size:94% position:6%
You're still looking into
his foundation.

00:02:40.293 --> 00:02:42.529 align:start size:94% position:6%
You were looking into
his university.

00:02:42.529 --> 00:02:45.532 align:start size:94% position:6%
But now you're actually
having to sue Donald Trump

00:02:45.532 --> 00:02:48.468 align:start size:94% position:6%
as a person who's representing
the federal government.

00:02:48.468 --> 00:02:50.670 align:start size:94% position:6%
Tell me some of the things
that you have had to do

00:02:50.670 --> 00:02:53.873
to defend against
Donald Trump's actions already.

00:02:53.873 --> 00:02:56.709
-Oh, sure.
Well, in terms of public policy,

00:02:56.709 --> 00:02:59.946 align:start size:94% position:6%
we have sued them
over their refusal

00:02:59.946 --> 00:03:02.515 align:start size:94% position:6%
to keep toxic pesticides
out of kids' food.

00:03:02.515 --> 00:03:05.718 align:start size:94% position:6%
We have sued them
for their efforts

00:03:05.718 --> 00:03:08.054 align:start size:94% position:6%
to dismantle
the cost-sharing subsidies

00:03:08.054 --> 00:03:09.989 align:start size:94% position:6%
under the Affordable Care Act,
Obamacare,

00:03:09.989 --> 00:03:12.692
which is still, as we sit here
tonight, the law of the land.

00:03:12.692 --> 00:03:15.395 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yeah. We'll see how --
We'll see how long.

00:03:15.395 --> 00:03:17.397 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yeah.
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:03:17.397 --> 00:03:18.932 line:92%
And I think will remain so.

00:03:18.932 --> 00:03:20.533 line:92%
But the Trump administration

00:03:20.533 --> 00:03:22.802 align:start size:94% position:6%
won't defend any
of the Obama-era policies.

00:03:22.802 --> 00:03:24.938 line:92%
So, I have intervened and sued,

00:03:24.938 --> 00:03:26.606 align:start size:94% position:6%
and other A.G.'s
have intervened and sued.

00:03:26.606 --> 00:03:28.575 align:start size:94% position:6%
We are taking up the cause
where --

00:03:28.575 --> 00:03:31.277 align:start size:94% position:6%
They won't defend any
of the Obama era's policies

00:03:31.277 --> 00:03:31.978 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
on climate change.

00:03:31.978 --> 00:03:33.980 size:84% position:42%
You mentioned the EPA
at the top of the show.

00:03:33.980 --> 00:03:36.015 align:start size:94% position:6%
They got a bunch
of climate-change deniers

00:03:36.015 --> 00:03:36.950 size:78% position:39% line:92%
in charge of the EPA.

00:03:36.950 --> 00:03:40.320 size:84% position:42%
So we are now defending
the Clean Power Plan,

00:03:40.320 --> 00:03:41.521 line:92%
other Obama-era initiatives,

00:03:41.521 --> 00:03:43.523 align:start size:94% position:6%
and we're suing them
for their failure

00:03:43.523 --> 00:03:44.958 align:start size:94% position:6%
to provide protection
for students

00:03:44.958 --> 00:03:47.994
who get ripped off by still
existing for-profit colleges.

00:03:47.994 --> 00:03:50.930 align:start size:94% position:6%
So we're going after them.
But it's all policy.

00:03:50.930 --> 00:03:52.732 line:92%
It's not about him personally.

00:03:52.732 --> 00:03:53.566 size:84% position:42% line:92%
It's all on the merits,

00:03:53.566 --> 00:03:56.736 align:start size:94% position:6%
but there are a lot of merits
these days, yeah.

00:03:56.736 --> 00:03:58.271 line:92%
-You talk about, you know,

00:03:58.271 --> 00:04:00.707 align:start size:94% position:6%
one of the things you're doing
is defending.

00:04:00.707 --> 00:04:01.407 line:92%
You're defending policies

00:04:01.407 --> 00:04:03.109 align:start size:94% position:6%
and the legal basis
of those policies.

00:04:03.109 --> 00:04:04.978 align:start size:94% position:6%
It seems like
what people want of you,

00:04:04.978 --> 00:04:07.480 size:81% position:41%
what a certain amount
of people want of you,

00:04:07.480 --> 00:04:09.148 align:start size:94% position:6%
is that your
legal investigation,

00:04:09.148 --> 00:04:12.252
your legal work will lead
to some grand impeachment,

00:04:12.252 --> 00:04:17.557
that this is one of the things
that people like you need to do.

00:04:17.557 --> 00:04:18.725 line:92%
Is it sort of wishful thinking?

00:04:18.725 --> 00:04:22.095
And do Democrats in general
need to step back from this idea

00:04:22.095 --> 00:04:24.430 align:start size:94% position:6%
that impeachment is something
that's going to happen

00:04:24.430 --> 00:04:25.632 align:start size:94% position:6%
and that impeachment
is something

00:04:25.632 --> 00:04:27.267 align:start size:94% position:6%
that's going to come about
by legal means?

00:04:27.267 --> 00:04:29.402 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Well, no. I think
you have to separate it out.

00:04:29.402 --> 00:04:31.971 align:start size:94% position:6%
Our first job is to protect
the people we represent

00:04:31.971 --> 00:04:33.439 align:start size:94% position:6%
from these horrendous
public policies

00:04:33.439 --> 00:04:37.844 align:start size:94% position:6%
that pour out of Washington
like a bad-idea toxic volcano.

00:04:37.844 --> 00:04:39.646
I mean, every day, there's
some new bad public policy

00:04:39.646 --> 00:04:42.048 align:start size:94% position:6%
that would hurt people.
We're going to protect them.

00:04:42.048 --> 00:04:45.285 align:start size:94% position:6%
As to misconduct
by the Trump campaign

00:04:45.285 --> 00:04:46.552 align:start size:94% position:6%
colluding with Russia
or, you know,

00:04:46.552 --> 00:04:49.956
allegations of money laundering
by people around the president,

00:04:49.956 --> 00:04:51.624 align:start size:94% position:6%
those are separate
investigations.

00:04:51.624 --> 00:04:52.725 size:81% position:41% line:92%
Those are going forth.

00:04:52.725 --> 00:04:53.626 line:92%
But I do think it is important

00:04:53.626 --> 00:04:56.396
for Democrats to recognize
the there is no substitute

00:04:56.396 --> 00:04:59.766
for the hard work at the end of
the day of electing good people.

00:04:59.766 --> 00:05:01.367 size:81% position:41%
And we have to go back
and elect good people

00:05:01.367 --> 00:05:05.104 size:81% position:41%
from the grassroots up
in order to get this
country back on track.

00:05:05.104 --> 00:05:06.906 size:84% position:42% line:92%
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:05:06.906 --> 00:05:09.575 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
-I'm...

00:05:10.843 --> 00:05:11.711 size:75% position:38% line:92%
Let it never be said

00:05:11.711 --> 00:05:13.513 size:81% position:41%
that attorney generals
can't have some fun.

00:05:13.513 --> 00:05:16.482 align:start size:94% position:6%
I want -- If you could,
real quick, explain to us.

00:05:16.482 --> 00:05:18.017 align:start size:94% position:6%
You had an
Operation Wrecking Ball?

00:05:18.017 --> 00:05:19.886 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Uh, we did.
-And can you tell us

00:05:19.886 --> 00:05:22.388
how you came to the title
Operation Wrecking Ball,

00:05:22.388 --> 00:05:23.222 line:92%
how you came to name it that?

00:05:23.222 --> 00:05:26.726
-Yeah, this was an Organized
Crime Task Force investigation

00:05:26.726 --> 00:05:32.699
of a gang that was dealing guns
and drugs in upstate New York.

00:05:32.699 --> 00:05:36.402 align:start size:94% position:6%
And they apparently
were Miley Cyrus fans.

00:05:36.402 --> 00:05:40.006 align:start size:94% position:6%
And their -- The code word
for cocaine was "Miley Cyrus."

00:05:40.006 --> 00:05:42.475 line:92%
So we took a Miley Cyrus song,

00:05:42.475 --> 00:05:44.043 align:start size:94% position:6%
called it
Operation Wrecking Ball,

00:05:44.043 --> 00:05:45.745 size:84% position:42% line:92%
and busted all of them.

00:05:45.745 --> 00:05:47.880
-Well, congratulations on that.
-Thank you.

00:05:47.880 --> 00:05:49.248 align:start size:94% position:6%
-And thank you
for all your hard work.

00:05:49.248 --> 00:05:51.784
Keep it up. And thank you
so much for being here.

00:05:51.784 --> 00:05:52.418 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
-Thank you, Seth.

00:05:52.418 --> 00:05:55.254 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Attorney General
Eric Schneiderman, everybody.

